# ===========================================================================================================
# Unity: folders Unity regenerates when the project is opened (never commit these)
# Library/ also holds the Multiplayer Play Mode virtual players (Library/VP).
# ===========================================================================================================
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
/[Rr]ecordings/
/.utmp/

# Builds and packages (the Quest APK is ~390 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB file limit)
*.apk
*.aab
*.obb
*.idsig
*.symbols.zip
*.unitypackage
*_BurstDebugInformation_DoNotShip/
*_BackUpThisFolder_ButDontShipItWithYourGame/

# Android signing keys: keep them outside the repository
*.keystore
*.jks

# IDE / OS files
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
.gradle/
.consulo/
ExportedObj/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.slnx
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.DotSettings.user
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta
sysinfo.txt
mono_crash.*
crashlytics-buildid.txt
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Asset .meta files are always committed (they hold the GUIDs scenes use to reference assets)
!/[Aa]ssets/**/*.meta

# Files the editor drops into Assets: the Rider plugin, and the scenes play-mode tests leave behind
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*
/[Aa]ssets/[Ii]nit[Tt]est[Ss]cene*.unity*

# ===========================================================================================================
# Over GitHub's 100 MB file limit - and regenerated automatically, so nothing is lost:
# Meta Avatars SDK preset avatars (944 MB; PresetAvatars_Quest.zip alone is 161 MB). The first time the project
# is opened, the Avatars SDK copies them out of the com.meta.xr.sdk.avatars.sample.assets package and packages
# the PresetAvatars_*.zip files again. No scene or prefab references these files by GUID (only by name).
# ===========================================================================================================
/[Aa]ssets/Oculus/Avatar2_SampleAssets/
/[Aa]ssets/Oculus/Avatar2_SampleAssets.meta

# The Avatars SDK copies the preset zips into StreamingAssets only while building and removes them afterwards
/[Aa]ssets/StreamingAssets/SampleAssets/
/[Aa]ssets/StreamingAssets/SampleAssets.meta

# ===========================================================================================================
# Package samples imported into Assets/Samples (Package Manager > Samples > Import).
# They ARE committed, because the project's own code and prefabs depend on them:
#   - Meta Avatars SDK "Sample Scenes": SampleAvatarEntity, OvrAvatarAnimationBehavior, and the humanoid rig
#     with its default animations in Scenes/LegsNetworkLoopback (used by Assets/Prefabs/AvatarNGOMeta.prefab).
#   - Vivox "Chat Channel Sample": VivoxVoiceManager (used by Assets/Scripts/Audio/VivoxPlayer.cs).
# Only the sample environments are left out (120 MB; Directional_flipped.hdr alone is 76 MB). Nothing outside
# the Meta sample scenes references them, and importing the sample again restores them with the same GUIDs.
# ===========================================================================================================
/[Aa]ssets/Samples/Meta Avatars SDK/*/Sample Scenes/Environments/
/[Aa]ssets/Samples/Meta Avatars SDK/*/Sample Scenes/Environments.meta
